I'm Amanda and I live yoga this is your  at-home yoga workout for runners we're  gonna start out with a dynamics forward  fold so you're gonna bring your  fingertips down to the mat bend your  knees enough so those hands can come  down so you're gonna start to straighten  and bend at the knees this is very  dynamic you don't want to have a static  pose here especially if you're warming  up for running so you want to keep the  legs nice and active bend and straighten  a few times like that I'm gonna step  that left foot back and again start to  straighten and Bend that front right  knee warming up the hip flexor warming  up the quad warming up the hamstring  next you're gonna take the right arm up  give yourself a little bit of a twist  here so you can start to straighten and  Bend that leg again now you've moved to  the IT band the outside of the leg and  into the knee few times like that hands  gonna come down left knee taps down you  walk your right foot slightly forward  hand on top of the knee now you're in a  crescent lunge here back foot is still  engaged and toe is tucked  push the knee forwards and can stretch  in the left hip flexor me pushes forward  hips sink slightly down shoulders back  chest lifts right hand can go down to  the matter on your hip left arm up and  over the ear this is going to take you a  little bit deeper in the left hip flexor  a deeper stretch here both hands go down  we're gonna take into a quad stretch  so you reach back with your left hand  grab the top of the foot and pull that  heel in towards your butt slowly release  that most injuries happen when you  release the pose so you slowly release  whatever pose you're in and then you're  gonna walk your hands forward foot goes  forward toes go back chest is reaching  towards your right foot so now you're in  a hamstring stretch here  and it may look a little like this it  may look a little like this depending on  your flexibility and where you are this  stretch is gonna look different for  everybody and start to breathe here just  deep breaths in deep breaths out as you  keep pulling the hip back reaching chest  for it you want to think nose towards  toes I'm gonna rebound that knee bring  the foot down step to the top of your  mat and then switch sides you take a  nice forward fold at the top you can  grab opposite elbows let the head hang  you can interlace the hands behind the  back giving yourself a shoulder and  chest stretch here knees can be soft  especially if you have tight hamstrings  and release the arms and slowly come up  to a standing position just to recap we  started out with the dynamic forward  fold step back into a low lunge then a  low lunge twist we drop the back knee  down for Crescent lunge and we went into  a quad stretch into a straight leg  forward fold  we bent the knee standing forward fold  then we repeated on the left side that  is your at-home yoga workout for runners  subscribe so you don't miss out on any  other fighting weight episodes  you
 

